// ask-lane-router.fk — one ask door. A request arrives; this cell says which lane carries it,
// what that lane needs, and — when it cannot be carried — which single thing is missing.
//
// WHAT THIS ROUTES, named plainly. The body has three local-native generation lanes:
// llama3.2:3b through observe/metal-ask-run.bml, DeepSeek-V4-Flash through
// form-stdlib/ds4-query-channel.fk, and the KAT/qwen35moe carving in native/metal/kat-token-handle.fk.
// The registry (form-stdlib/native-model-control-plane.fk) knows all of them as rows. Each has its
// own carrier. Without this cell nothing routes a request BY the row — the caller would pick a
// carrier, and picking a carrier is picking an answer before asking a question.
//
// WHY THIS IS NOT A SWITCH, which is the design and not a defence. A switch is configuration chosen
// before the body runs: FORM_DS4_BLOB named one file out of six, so the body was TOLD its world
// instead of looking at it. Every input to this cell is either something only the caller can know
// (which lane of work, which modality, how many steps, whether the answer may leave the machine) or
// something the HOST REPORTED after looking (today's date, whether a Metal device answered, which
// GGUFs model-discovery.fk found and what architecture each file's own header declares, which carrier
// scripts exist, which runtimes are on PATH). The choice is made while the body runs, from options
// the body found. This cell adds no environment variable and no flag.
//
// THE THREE MEMBERS OF A ROUTE, and why a lane needs all three. This is the whole shape:
//
//   the ROW      the registry's witness statement — this lane exists, it is active, it was witnessed
//                on a day, its status is proven or observed or partial. AUTHORITY: may it answer.
//   the BLOB     a file on this host whose own header declares the architecture. GROUND: the bytes
//                are here. A row without a blob is a claim about somewhere else.
//   the CARRIER  a script this body wrote that carves that architecture. THE HAND: something can run
//                it. A row and a blob with no carrier is arithmetic nobody has hands for.
//
// A route is CARRIED when all three join and every derived need is met. Otherwise UNFINISHED, with
// the missing member named. There is no third verdict, and `alr-status?` does not carry one: Urs, 2026-08-03,
// "we support all silicon on all platforms, and if we find an issue that means unfinished work,
// nothing more" and "the only limit are the physical hardware and our imagination". A router that can
// say "unsupported" will eventually say it about work that was merely undone, so the word is absent
// from the type.
//
// WHY THE BINDINGS ARE A WITNESSED LIST AND NOT A DERIVATION. A registry row names a model
// ("DeepSeek-V4-Flash-REAP25-DSpark"); a GGUF on disk names a file
// (ds4flash-v5mx-reap25-type40-mxfp8lt-dspark-v1.gguf); the join between them is the ARCHITECTURE the
// file's header declares (deepseek4). I tried to derive that key from the model name by taking its
// leading token, and it is wrong on this very host: "DeepSeek-V4-..." lowercases to "deepseek", which
// matches the IQ2XXS chat blob and NOT the reap25 blob the lane actually runs. A derivation that is
// wrong on the first three cases is a guess wearing a function's name. So `alr-bindings` is a
// witnessed inventory in the same discipline as `nmcp-registry`: dated, correctable, and each row
// verifiable by reading the carrier that keys on that architecture.
//
// WHAT THIS CELL DOES NOT SPEAK FOR (aporon). It does not generate a token. It does not verify that
// the carrier it names will succeed — a present script and a present blob are necessary, never
// sufficient, and the carrier's own witnesses remain the proof that it computed anything. It does not
// adjudicate whether the blob it found is the SAME quantization the lane was witnessed against; three
// deepseek4 files sit on this host and this cell picks the first the host reported, which is a real
// seam named in the receipt rather than hidden behind a preference nobody wrote down.
//
// witnessed 2026-08-03 on M4 Max: six GGUFs under ~/models across three architectures —
// qwen35moe (41 layers), deepseek4 (43), llama (28) — read by model-discovery.fk from each file's
// own header, not from a list.
//
// preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk, form-stdlib/native-model-control-plane.fk
//
// Proven by: form-stdlib/tests/ask-lane-router-band.fk
section [form.bml] {
    // ---- the ask. Only the caller knows these; they are arguments, not knobs. ----------------
    //   lane        the lane of work, matched against the registry row's own lane field
    //   modality    text / audio / image / multimodal
    //   steps       how far to walk. A cap, not a length.
    //   floor       the least status this answer will accept: 3 proven, 2 observed, 1 partial
    //   off-host?   may this question leave the machine. Consent, and nobody else can give it.
    def alr-ask(lane, modality, steps, floor, off-host) = ["alr-ask", lane, modality, steps, floor, off-host];
    def alr-ask?(a) = (Comparable) len(a) == 6 && (String) a[0] == "alr-ask" ? 1 : 0;
    def alr-ask-lane(a) = a[1];
    def alr-ask-modality(a) = a[2];
    def alr-ask-steps(a) = a[3];
    def alr-ask-floor(a) = a[4];
    def alr-ask-off-host?(a) = a[5];
    // ---- what the host reported, after looking. Observation, never configuration. ------------
    // A blob is what model-discovery.fk returns for one file: its path, the architecture its OWN
    // header declares, and the block count under that architecture's key.
    def alr-blob(path, arch, layers) = ["alr-blob", path, arch, layers];
    def alr-blob?(b) = (Comparable) len(b) == 4 && (String) b[0] == "alr-blob" ? 1 : 0;
    def alr-blob-path(b) = b[1];
    def alr-blob-arch(b) = b[2];
    def alr-blob-layers(b) = b[3];
    // A carrier is a script this body wrote, present on this host, that carves one architecture.
    def alr-carrier(path, arch) = ["alr-carrier", path, arch];
    def alr-carrier?(c) = (Comparable) len(c) == 3 && (String) c[0] == "alr-carrier" ? 1 : 0;
    def alr-carrier-path(c) = c[1];
    def alr-carrier-arch(c) = c[2];
    def alr-host(day, metal, blobs, carriers, runtimes) = ["alr-host", day, metal, blobs, carriers, runtimes];
    def alr-host?(h) = (Comparable) len(h) == 6 && (String) h[0] == "alr-host" ? 1 : 0;
    def alr-host-day(h) = h[1];
    def alr-host-metal?(h) = h[2];
    def alr-host-blobs(h) = h[3];
    def alr-host-carriers(h) = h[4];
    def alr-host-runtimes(h) = h[5];
    // ---- the binding. Registry row id -> the architecture its recipe carves. -------------------
    // Verifiable by reading the carrier: kat-token-handle.fk keys on qwen35moe.block_count and
    // qwen35moe.full_attention_interval; every other bind is checkable against the row it names.
    //
    // AND WHY THE BIND CARRIES A KEY AS WELL AS AN ARCHITECTURE.  The first version joined on
    // architecture alone, and the live run refuted it in one line: asked for general-text it returned
    // CARRIED on /Users/ursmuff/models/form-llama-vital-ground-f16.gguf, because that file's header
    // says `llama` and so does llama3.2:3b's.  They are not the same model — one is a form-trained
    // checkpoint, the other the champion row's witnessed weights — and a router that hands a lane the
    // wrong weights while reporting success is worse than one that says not yet.  An architecture says how
    // a file is RUN; it does not say WHICH model it is.  So a bind also carries a key: a
    // substring that needs to appear in the path.  An empty key means any file of that architecture will
    // do, and it is a claim, not a default — say it only where it is true.
    def alr-bind(id, arch, key) = ["alr-bind", id, arch, key];
    def alr-bind-id(b) = b[1];
    def alr-bind-arch(b) = b[2];
    def alr-bind-key(b) = b[3];
    def alr-no-bind() = alr-bind("", "", "");
    def alr-bindings() = list(    // the champion's weights are ollama's content-addressed blob; the registry row carries
    // that same sha256 in its artifact field, so the key is checkable against the row.
alr-bind("base.llama32-3b-metal", "llama", "dde5aa3fc5ffc171"),     // the row names REAP25 in its model field.
alr-bind("challenger.deepseek-ds4-metal", "deepseek4", "reap25"),     // Form-native Qwen3.8 generate. The key is the filename token, not the arch:
    // qwen35moe (KAT) is a different file and stays unbound until its own row vouches.
alr-bind("challenger.qwen38-27b-metal", "qwen35", "Qwen3.8"),     // a component row that has never answered an ask.  Its key is empty because no file has
    // been witnessed for it — when it answers, the key wants witnessing first.
alr-bind("llm.llama32-3b-gguf-partial", "llama", ""));
    // ---- small honest tools --------------------------------------------------------------------
    def alr-present?(s) = str_len(s) > 0 ? 1 : 0;
    def alr-name-in?(name, xs) = (Comparable) len(xs) == 0 ? 0 : (String) name == head(xs) ? 1 : alr-name-in?(name, tail(xs));
    def alr-has-metal?(runtime) = str_find(runtime, "Metal", 0) >= 0 ? 1 : 0;
    def alr-bind-of(id, binds) = (Comparable) len(binds) == 0 ? alr-no-bind() : (String) alr-bind-id(head(binds)) == id ? head(binds) : alr-bind-of(id, tail(binds));
    def alr-arch-of(id, binds) = alr-bind-arch(alr-bind-of(id, binds));
    // A blob answers a bind when its architecture matches AND its path carries the bind's key.  An
    // empty key matches anything, which is why an empty key is a claim about the lane and not a
    // shrug about the file.
    def alr-blob-answers?(blob, bind) = (String) alr-blob-arch(blob) == alr-bind-arch(bind) ? (Comparable) str_len(alr-bind-key(bind)) == 0 ? 1 : str_find(alr-blob-path(blob), alr-bind-key(bind), 0) >= 0 ? 1 : 0 : 0;
    def alr-blob-for(bind, blobs) = (Comparable) len(blobs) == 0 ? "" : (Comparable) alr-blob-answers?(head(blobs), bind) == 1 ? alr-blob-path(head(blobs)) : alr-blob-for(bind, tail(blobs));
    def alr-carrier-for(arch, carriers) = (Comparable) len(carriers) == 0 ? "" : (String) alr-carrier-arch(head(carriers)) == arch ? alr-carrier-path(head(carriers)) : alr-carrier-for(arch, tail(carriers));
    // ---- status, ranked. A lane that is failing, pending or historical never answers. ----------
    // trained-unpromoted sits with partial: the weights exist, the promotion did not happen, and a
    // caller who asked for proven is not handed it quietly.
    def alr-status-rank(s) = (String) s == "proven" ? 3 : (String) s == "observed" ? 2 : (String) s == "partial" ? 1 : (String) s == "trained-unpromoted" ? 1 : 0;
    def alr-surface-rank(s) = (String) s == "native-recipe" ? 3 : (String) s == "local-process" ? 2 : (String) s == "remote-membrane" ? 1 : 0;
    // ---- what a lane needs, derived from its own surface and runtime -------------------------
    // This is the answer to "what does that lane need", and it is read off the row rather than
    // attached to it, so a row that changes surface changes its needs in the same edit.
    def alr-needs(row) = (String) nmcp-surface(row) == "native-recipe" ? (Comparable) alr-has-metal?(nmcp-runtime(row)) == 1 ? ["fkwu", "metal-device", "model-blob", "carrier"] : ["fkwu", "recipe-cell"] : (String) nmcp-surface(row) == "local-process" ? ["host-process", nmcp-runtime(row)] : ["network", "call-ledger", "off-host-consent"];
    def alr-need-met?(need, ask, host, bind) = (String) need == "fkwu" ? 1 : (String) need == "recipe-cell" ? 1 : (String) need == "metal-device" ? alr-host-metal?(host) : (String) need == "model-blob" ? alr-present?(alr-blob-for(bind, alr-host-blobs(host))) : (String) need == "carrier" ? alr-present?(alr-carrier-for(alr-bind-arch(bind), alr-host-carriers(host))) : (String) need == "off-host-consent" ? alr-ask-off-host?(ask) : alr-name-in?(need, alr-host-runtimes(host));
    def alr-first-unmet(needs, ask, host, bind) = (Comparable) len(needs) == 0 ? "" : (Comparable) alr-need-met?(head(needs), ask, host, bind) == 1 ? alr-first-unmet(tail(needs), ask, host, bind) : head(needs);
    // ---- admission. Each threshold stands alone, so a decline can name which one closed. -------
    def alr-lane-match?(row, ask) = (String) nmcp-lane(row) == alr-ask-lane(ask) && (String) nmcp-modality(row) == alr-ask-modality(ask) ? 1 : 0;
    def alr-consent-ok?(row, ask) = (String) nmcp-surface(row) == "remote-membrane" ? (Comparable) alr-ask-off-host?(ask) == 1 ? 1 : 0 : 1;
    def alr-admissible?(row, ask, host) = (Comparable) alr-lane-match?(row, ask) == 1 ? (Comparable) nmcp-active?(row) == 1 ? (Comparable) nmcp-fresh?(row, alr-host-day(host)) == 1 ? alr-status-rank(nmcp-status(row)) >= alr-ask-floor(ask) ? alr-consent-ok?(row, ask) : 0 : 0 : 0 : 0;
    // The first threshold that closed, in the same order the predicate walks them.  A decline that
    // cannot say which membrane stopped it teaches the caller nothing.
    def alr-first-closed(row, ask, host) = (Comparable) alr-lane-match?(row, ask) == 0 ? "lane-or-modality" : (Comparable) nmcp-active?(row) == 0 ? "row-not-active" : (Comparable) nmcp-fresh?(row, alr-host-day(host)) == 0 ? "witness-stale" : alr-status-rank(nmcp-status(row)) < alr-ask-floor(ask) ? "status-below-floor" : (Comparable) alr-consent-ok?(row, ask) == 0 ? "off-host-consent" : "none";
    // ---- choosing. Status first, then how close to the metal, then witnessed priority. ---------
    // Ties keep the incumbent, so the fold is stable and the same registry always answers the same.
    def alr-better(a, b, ask, host) = (Comparable) alr-admissible?(a, ask, host) == 0 ? b : (Comparable) alr-admissible?(b, ask, host) == 0 ? a : alr-status-rank(nmcp-status(a)) > alr-status-rank(nmcp-status(b)) ? a : alr-status-rank(nmcp-status(a)) < alr-status-rank(nmcp-status(b)) ? b : alr-surface-rank(nmcp-surface(a)) > alr-surface-rank(nmcp-surface(b)) ? a : alr-surface-rank(nmcp-surface(a)) < alr-surface-rank(nmcp-surface(b)) ? b : nmcp-priority(a) > nmcp-priority(b) ? a : b;
    def alr-none-row() = nmcp-model("none", "none", "none", "form-native", "component", "pending", "native-recipe", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", 0, 0, 0, 0, "none", 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0);
    def alr-choose-loop(rows, best, ask, host) = (Comparable) len(rows) == 0 ? best : alr-choose-loop(tail(rows), alr-better(head(rows), best, ask, host), ask, host);
    def alr-choose(rows, ask, host) = alr-choose-loop(rows, alr-none-row(), ask, host);
    // The nearest miss: a row that wanted this lane but met a closed threshold.  Reported so an unfinished
    // route points at work rather than at a wall.
    def alr-near-miss-loop(rows, ask, host) = (Comparable) len(rows) == 0 ? alr-none-row() : (Comparable) alr-lane-match?(head(rows), ask) == 1 ? head(rows) : alr-near-miss-loop(tail(rows), ask, host);
    // ---- the route ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    def alr-route(status, id, arch, carrier, blob, needs, reason) = ["alr-route", status, id, arch, carrier, blob, needs, reason];
    def alr-route?(r) = (Comparable) len(r) == 8 && (String) r[0] == "alr-route" ? 1 : 0;
    def alr-route-status(r) = r[1];
    def alr-route-id(r) = r[2];
    def alr-route-arch(r) = r[3];
    def alr-route-carrier(r) = r[4];
    def alr-route-blob(r) = r[5];
    def alr-route-needs(r) = r[6];
    def alr-route-reason(r) = r[7];
    // Two verdicts, and the type carries no third.  See the header.
    def alr-status?(s) = (String) s == "carried" ? 1 : (String) s == "unfinished" ? 1 : 0;
    def alr-carried?(r) = (String) alr-route-status(r) == "carried" ? 1 : 0;
    def alr-unfinished(id, arch, needs, why) = alr-route("unfinished", id, arch, "", "", needs, why);
    // The route for one already-chosen row.  Split out so a caller who names a model by id gets the
    // same walk as a caller who let the registry choose.
    def alr-route-row(row, ask, host, binds) = (Comparable) alr-admissible?(row, ask, host) == 1 ? {
        let bind = alr-bind-of(nmcp-id(row), binds);
        let arch = alr-bind-arch(bind);
        let needs = alr-needs(row);
        (Comparable) alr-has-metal?(nmcp-runtime(row)) == 1 && (Comparable) alr-present?(arch) == 0 ? alr-unfinished(nmcp-id(row), "", needs, "no architecture is bound to this row; alr-bindings has not witnessed it") : {
            let missing = alr-first-unmet(needs, ask, host, bind);
            (Comparable) alr-present?(missing) == 1 ? alr-unfinished(nmcp-id(row), arch, needs, str_concat("this lane needs ", str_concat(missing, ", and this host did not report it"))) : alr-route("carried", nmcp-id(row), arch, alr-carrier-for(arch, alr-host-carriers(host)), alr-blob-for(bind, alr-host-blobs(host)), needs, "row, blob and carrier all joined");
        };
    } : alr-unfinished(nmcp-id(row), "", [], str_concat("this row cannot answer: ", alr-first-closed(row, ask, host)));
    // The door.  A request and a host report go in; a route comes out, always one of two verdicts.
    def alr-ask-door(rows, ask, host, binds) = {
        let best = alr-choose(rows, ask, host);
        (String) nmcp-id(best) == "none" ? {
            let near = alr-near-miss-loop(rows, ask, host);
            (String) nmcp-id(near) == "none" ? alr-unfinished("none", "", [], str_concat("no row in the registry carries the lane ", alr-ask-lane(ask))) : alr-unfinished(nmcp-id(near), "", [], str_concat("the nearest row cannot answer: ", alr-first-closed(near, ask, host)));
        } : alr-route-row(best, ask, host, binds);
    };
    // Naming a model directly: the caller chose an id, the registry still holds the authority.
    def alr-row-by-id(rows, id) = (Comparable) len(rows) == 0 ? alr-none-row() : (String) nmcp-id(head(rows)) == id ? head(rows) : alr-row-by-id(tail(rows), id);
    def alr-ask-door-by-id(rows, ask, host, binds, id) = {
        let row = alr-row-by-id(rows, id);
        (String) nmcp-id(row) == "none" ? alr-unfinished(id, "", [], str_concat("the registry holds no row with id ", id)) : alr-route-row(row, ask, host, binds);
    };
    // ---- the mirror. What this host can run that no row has vouched for. ------------------------
    // A blob whose architecture has a carrier and no bound registry row is capability the body has
    // and has not said it has.  qwen35moe is that case: kat-token-handle.fk carves it, the file is
    // on disk, and alr-bindings binds no lane to it.  Surfacing it here is the difference between a
    // router and a switchboard.
    def alr-vouched?(arch, binds, rows) = (Comparable) len(binds) == 0 ? 0 : (String) alr-bind-arch(head(binds)) == arch ? (String) nmcp-id(alr-row-by-id(rows, alr-bind-id(head(binds)))) == "none" ? alr-vouched?(arch, tail(binds), rows) : 1 : alr-vouched?(arch, tail(binds), rows);
    def alr-unvouched-loop(blobs, host, binds, rows, acc) = (Comparable) len(blobs) == 0 ? acc : {
        let arch = alr-blob-arch(head(blobs));
        alr-unvouched-loop(tail(blobs), host, binds, rows, (Comparable) alr-present?(alr-carrier-for(arch, alr-host-carriers(host))) == 1 && ((Comparable) alr-vouched?(arch, binds, rows) == 0 && (Comparable) alr-name-in?(arch, acc) == 0) ? cons(arch, acc) : acc);
    };
    def alr-unvouched(host, binds, rows) = alr-unvouched-loop(alr-host-blobs(host), host, binds, rows, []);
    // ---- saying it out loud ---------------------------------------------------------------------
    def alr-say-needs(xs) = (Comparable) len(xs) == 0 ? 0 : {
        print_str(str_concat("    needs   ", head(xs)));
        alr-say-needs(tail(xs));
    };
    def alr-say-route(r) = {
        print_str(str_concat("— route: ", alr-route-status(r)));
        print_str(str_concat("    row     ", alr-route-id(r)));
        print_str(str_concat("    arch    ", alr-route-arch(r)));
        print_str(str_concat("    carrier ", alr-route-carrier(r)));
        print_str(str_concat("    blob    ", alr-route-blob(r)));
        alr-say-needs(alr-route-needs(r));
        print_str(str_concat("    because ", alr-route-reason(r)));
        alr-carried?(r);
    };
    0;
}
